# Doton-OS

> **An open operating system ecosystem for anyone.**

Doton-OS is an open operating system ecosystem consisting of the Doton Microkernel, Doublers Instruction Set Architecture (ISA), LinkLoader Runtime Manager, Deshell (DSH), and the Deson Compiler Specification. Its purpose is not to replace existing operating systems, but to provide an independent operating system ecosystem with its own specifications that anyone may study, implement, improve, and build upon.

---

# Components
- 🖥️ Doton Microkernel - ⚙️ Doublers ISA - 🔗 LinkLoader - 💻 Deshell (DSH) - 🛣️ Deson Compiler - 📜 Doton-OS Package License (DPL)

---

# Goals
- Create an independent operating system ecosystem. - Encourage compatible operating system implementations. - Preserve long-term specification compatibility. - Allow the community to improve the specifications while preserving their original meaning. - Provide an open ecosystem for learning, research, and development.
---

# Community
Anyone may:
- Read the specifications. - Study the operating system ecosystem. - Build compatible kernels. - Build compatible software. - Improve the official specifications while preserving their original architectural meaning. - Create compatible extensions.
See the **Doton-OS Package License (DPL)** for complete licensing terms.
---

# Compatibility
Any implementation claiming compatibility with the official Doton-OS ecosystem shall preserve the behavior defined by the official specifications.
Community improvements to the documentation are encouraged, provided they do not change the meaning or compatibility of the specifications.
